# WorkTruth environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the repo root and fill in real values:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored — never commit real secrets to this file.
# It is loaded automatically by:
#   - the API server (artifacts/api-server) at startup
#   - the frontend (artifacts/worktruth) at dev/build config time
#   - `pnpm --filter db run push` / `push-force`
#   - `pnpm db:seed`

# PostgreSQL connection string. Required — there is no local default because
# it always points at a specific database instance.
#
# This matches the docker-compose.yml LOCAL DEVELOPMENT default exactly —
# after `docker compose up -d --wait`, this value works as-is. Never reuse
# these credentials for a staging/production database.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://worktruth:worktruth_dev_password@localhost:5432/worktruth

# TLS for `pnpm db:migrate` (lib/db/src/migrate.ts) only — optional, "require"
# or "disable". Leave unset: it's auto-detected from DATABASE_URL's host
# (localhost -> no TLS, matching docker-compose; any other host, e.g. Render
# -> TLS). Set this only if that auto-detection ever guesses wrong for a
# particular target.
# DATABASE_SSL=require

# Port the Express API server listens on. Optional — defaults to 5000.
# In production the host platform (Render, etc.) injects PORT; leave it to do so.
PORT=5000

# Node environment. Leave unset locally. Set to `production` on the deployed
# API service — it makes the session cookie Secure, and (with SEED_DEMO_DATA
# unset) stops the 20 demo projects from ever being auto-created in a real
# database.
# NODE_ENV=production

# Interface the API binds to. Optional — defaults to 0.0.0.0 (all interfaces),
# which is what Render and other container hosts require. Set to 127.0.0.1
# only for a loopback-only local setup.
# HOST=0.0.0.0

# Port the Vite frontend dev/preview server listens on. Optional — defaults
# to 5173. Named WEB_PORT (not PORT) so the frontend and the API server can
# run at the same time under `pnpm dev` without fighting over one variable.
WEB_PORT=5173

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend production build (Render Static Site) — build-time only
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Absolute origin of the deployed API, e.g. https://worktruth-api.onrender.com
# Unset locally: the frontend calls relative /api/... paths and the Vite dev
# proxy forwards them to the local API. Set at BUILD time for production so the
# static bundle calls the real API origin directly.
# This value is inlined into the public JS bundle — it is a URL, not a secret.
# NEVER put a password, token, or connection string in any VITE_* variable.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://worktruth-api.onrender.com

# Officer account. Provisioned (created, or its password rotated to match)
# every time the seed logic runs — on first API request, and on `pnpm db:seed`
# — whenever all three are set. This is real operator identity, so it is
# created in production too; the demo PROJECTS below are what production skips.
# There is no built-in login — without these set, no account exists.
# Pick your own values. Do NOT reuse the placeholder password below.
SEED_OFFICER_EMAIL=officer@example.com
SEED_OFFICER_NAME=Duty Officer
SEED_OFFICER_PASSWORD=change-this-password

# Optional admin account, provisioned the same idempotent way as the officer
# account above (same create/rotate-password-only/no-op logic — see
# ensureSeedAccount in artifacts/api-server/src/lib/worktruth.ts). Not
# required: WorkTruth works with only the officer account above. Set these
# when you need a first ADMIN to sign in and use Admin User Management
# (/admin/users) to create every other account from inside the app —
# otherwise there is no way to create the very first admin. Do NOT hard-code
# a real password anywhere; set it only here (or in your host's secret
# store) and never commit a real value.
# SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
# SEED_ADMIN_NAME=System Administrator
# SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-this-password-too

# Whether the 20-project demo dataset may be auto-seeded.
#   unset  -> seeded in local dev; NOT seeded when NODE_ENV=production
#   true   -> always seeded (use to deliberately populate a demo/staging DB)
#   false  -> never seeded
# `pnpm db:seed` honors this too.
# SEED_DEMO_DATA=false

# Directory where uploaded evidence images are stored on the local
# filesystem. Optional — defaults to ./uploads relative to where the API
# server process runs (artifacts/api-server/uploads).
# IN PRODUCTION THIS MUST POINT AT A PERSISTENT VOLUME (the default path is on
# the ephemeral container filesystem and is wiped on every redeploy/restart).
# On Render: mount a disk at /var/data and set EVIDENCE_UPLOAD_DIR=/var/data/uploads
# (the directory is created on first upload; path-traversal checks are unchanged).
# EVIDENCE_UPLOAD_DIR=./uploads

# Exact browser origin(s) the frontend is served from, when it is a DIFFERENT
# origin than this API (e.g. a Render Static Site calling a Render Web Service).
# Comma-separate to allow more than one. Enabling this also switches the
# session cookie to SameSite=None; Secure so it survives cross-origin XHR.
# Leave unset for local dev — the Vite proxy makes /api same-origin there, so
# CORS never applies. Never use "*".
# CORS_ORIGIN=https://worktruth-web.onrender.com

# SESSION_SECRET is NOT currently used and does not need to be set. Sessions
# are opaque, random, server-generated tokens stored in the database
# (see artifacts/api-server/src/lib/auth.ts) — there is no cookie-signing or
# JWT secret anywhere in the login/session flow to configure. This variable
# is documented here only so its absence isn't mistaken for a missing
# requirement; it is intentionally not read by any code.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional external APIs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The core WorkTruth analysis pipeline currently runs without an external AI
# API. The financial, geospatial, temporal, text, and visual engines, the
# evidence-fusion, cross-modal-inconsistency, and verification-priority
# engines are all deterministic, local computations (see
# artifacts/api-server/src/lib/*-engine.ts) — none of them call out to any
# third-party service, so there is nothing to configure here today.
